                        "form": "palliest"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "ed38b0ce-3f82-4d98-a6ee-2559d075c691",
                        "entry_id": "084d59d8-2cfc-3295-b65d-09d9eb6ba733",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most pally"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "028ad8f1-2cf9-3216-9a68-b6ecafe9853d",
                        "entry_id": "084d59d8-2cfc-3295-b65d-09d9eb6ba733",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Like a pal; friendly."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "182f74f9-d944-4424-b4ac-0835cea0c476",
                                "sense_id": "028ad8f1-2cf9-3216-9a68-b6ecafe9853d",
                                "text": "The O′Briens are the palliest of pals with the Prince of Wales and when HRH is in Biarritz he and Jay are inseparable."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8f88ac16-f62e-48fd-9b7a-6240e42dbeb1",
                                "sense_id": "028ad8f1-2cf9-3216-9a68-b6ecafe9853d",
                                "text": "Words are the friendliest and palliest things I know."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0e9c57b9-e9c6-42e6-96f6-6c8a9137160f",
                                "sense_id": "028ad8f1-2cf9-3216-9a68-b6ecafe9853d",
                                "text": "[…]he was a champion boozer and the palliest bloke in the pub."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8521dac4-c607-4f34-806e-43b10645128e",
                                "sense_id": "028ad8f1-2cf9-3216-9a68-b6ecafe9853d",
                                "text": "2006, Vidar Helgesen, Erik Solheim, The Straight Talkers, Harriet Martin (editor), Kofi Atta Annan (foreword), Kings of Peace, Pawns of War: The Untold Story of Peace-Making, page 112,\nAnd with each round the two negotiating teams got more and more pally. ‘By the sixth round we were having Jacuzzis together!’"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0af12085-8e79-40eb-8b72-852cb60ffb7f",
                                "sense_id": "028ad8f1-2cf9-3216-9a68-b6ecafe9853d",
                                "text": "When there were Australian officers everyone was more pally and sociable which made it easier for the lady in charge to entertain the party."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d7f3239c-82b0-4eb7-941f-acc607a6747f",
                                "sense_id": "028ad8f1-2cf9-3216-9a68-b6ecafe9853d",
                                "text": "The chap I′m most pally with is Fright who is nearly sixty now but still climbs like a youngster."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "ba7b49fc-9eee-3e7f-9698-1d05c0c09e98",
                "word": "pally",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "b1514882-35a3-45e9-9077-7d10cf789e00",
                        "entry_id": "ba7b49fc-9eee-3e7f-9698-1d05c0c09e98",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "pallies"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "18c9e8af-5ed5-36e6-b40d-77b8d0146ee1",
                        "entry_id": "ba7b49fc-9eee-3e7f-9698-1d05c0c09e98",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An affectionate term of address."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "US"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "be1099ea-89cc-4be3-8dd1-e758ec5e73f9",
                                "sense_id": "18c9e8af-5ed5-36e6-b40d-77b8d0146ee1",
                                "text": "‘Sit here, pally.’ He pushed me down."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e21b7455-d022-4e69-adae-614a7adf03da",
                                "sense_id": "18c9e8af-5ed5-36e6-b40d-77b8d0146ee1",
                                "text": "Well, a lot of water has flown under the bridges since then, pally, and while I have been laying off lately, I′m still the same old Joey, which is more than I can say for that O′Hara creep."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1aa1d7f0-d7c6-47a0-87b0-a474f2d9d8e3",
                                "sense_id": "18c9e8af-5ed5-36e6-b40d-77b8d0146ee1",
                                "text": "Ahmed the Turk grinned. “You call this hot, chommy? Pally, we used to take slices off the heat, put them on our biscuits and make toast.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7b489d05-bc42-4ebc-9057-de42d835fc84",
                                "sense_id": "18c9e8af-5ed5-36e6-b40d-77b8d0146ee1",
                                "text": "As the Giants moved West, most accepted Horace Stoneham′s apologia: “I can′t stay where I am, pally. If I don′t move the team I go bankrupt. Except for Chub [Feeney], all my relatives would starve.”"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f410d079-4024-363c-ac09-6a6f556b2da5",
                        "entry_id": "ba7b49fc-9eee-3e7f-9698-1d05c0c09e98",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A slightly derogatory and insulting term of address."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Australia",
                            "US"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9ddd794f-aa44-453a-8cba-84f732937871",
                                "sense_id": "f410d079-4024-363c-ac09-6a6f556b2da5",
                                "text": "What do you think you are doing, pally?"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
